{"jdk":"26","running_on":"26.0.1+8","version":"1.0.0","jeps":[{"jep":517,"title":"HTTP/3 for the HTTP Client API","status":"Final","where":"com.kangaroo.infer.OpenAiCompatibleEngine","why":"The cloud rung runs over QUIC with ALT_SVC discovery. On a rural mobile link, per-stream loss recovery and connection migration are what let an upload survive packet loss and a cell handover instead of restarting.","load_bearing":true},{"jep":525,"title":"Structured Concurrency","status":"Preview","where":"com.kangaroo.orchestrate.AssessmentOrchestrator","why":"The four evidence passes fan out into one scope with one deadline and one cancellation domain, so a slow visual pass cannot eat the audio pass's budget and an abandoned encounter leaves no orphan threads.","load_bearing":true},{"jep":526,"title":"Lazy Constants","status":"Preview","where":"com.kangaroo.clinical.Reference, com.kangaroo.ml.Models","why":"The WHO tables and both gradient-boosted models load on first use and are constant-folded afterwards. A device that only runs the deterministic path never pays to parse 1.5 MB of trees.","load_bearing":true},{"jep":530,"title":"Primitive Types in Patterns, instanceof, and switch","status":"Preview","where":"com.kangaroo.ml.Tree, com.kangaroo.ml.GbmModel","why":"LightGBM's decision_type is a packed byte, unpacked as a switch over the primitive with checked coverage. And `threshold instanceof float` is a checked narrowing that tells us which trees are genuinely float-safe.","load_bearing":false},{"jep":529,"title":"Vector API","status":"Incubator","where":"com.kangaroo.color.VectorPipeline","why":"The colorimetry kernels run over FloatVector.SPECIES_PREFERRED, with mask-and-reduce replacing a branch per pixel and Vector.compress packing the selected skin pixels. Measured live at /api/bench.","load_bearing":true},{"jep":524,"title":"PEM Encodings of Cryptographic Objects","status":"Preview","where":"com.kangaroo.crypto.DeviceIdentity","why":"Ed25519 device identity and per-record signatures. PEM is what you paste into an enrolment form, and PEMEncoder makes reading and writing it a standard library call instead of a cryptography dependency.","load_bearing":true},{"jep":516,"title":"Ahead-of-Time Object Caching with Any GC","status":"Final","where":"packaging/aot.sh, packaging/aot.ps1","why":"A two-run training and use cycle produces an AOT cache shipped alongside the installer. JEP 516 is precisely what lifts the earlier GC restriction, so the cache and the production collector can be used together.","load_bearing":false},{"jep":522,"title":"G1 GC: Improve Throughput by Reducing Synchronization","status":"Final","where":"packaging/gc-benchmark.sh","why":"The Pod serves a dozen phones concurrently, which is the allocation pattern this JEP improves. Measured on identical hardware across JDK 25 and 26.","load_bearing":false},{"jep":500,"title":"Prepare to Make Final Mean Final","status":"Final","where":"pom.xml, packaging/run.sh","why":"The application runs under --illegal-final-field-access=deny. For clinical software, 'no library can quietly mutate a final field in the dosing table' is a safety property rather than a checkbox.","load_bearing":false},{"jep":504,"title":"Remove the Applet API","status":"Final (removal)","where":"the whole dependency graph","why":"Nothing in this project touches java.applet, because the runtime dependency set is exactly the JDK. Kangaroo builds on 26 unmodified.","load_bearing":false}],"foundations":[{"jep":454,"title":"Foreign Function & Memory API","status":"Final since 22","where":"com.kangaroo.ffm.llama","why":"The entire native layer. No JNI anywhere in the repository.","load_bearing":true},{"jep":444,"title":"Virtual Threads","status":"Final since 21","where":"com.kangaroo.http.KangarooServer","why":"Thread per request, so a request that blocks in a model for eight seconds costs a few hundred bytes rather than a pooled platform thread.","load_bearing":true},{"jep":409,"title":"Sealed Classes","status":"